// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`handoff for each demo scenario > plain text matches snapshot: asl-fall 1`] = `
"FirstWords handoff to the emergency department
Patient, about 74 years old, female
Communication: ASL interpreter needed on arrival. Language: American Sign Language. Preferred mode: ASL. Until the interpreter arrives, use written English, pictures, and yes or no questions.
M: Chief complaint: A fall or injury; Mechanism: Fall while: on the stairs; Onset: 20 minutes ago (about 13:40)
I: Location: Head, Back; Head strike: Yes
S: Quality: Dull ache; Pain: 5 out of 10; Radiates to: Does not spread; Better or worse with: Moving makes it worse; Vitals: HR 88, BP 146/82, SpO2 97%, RR 16
T: Given: C-collar
Allergies: No allergies
Medications: apixaban (Eliquis), Anticoagulant (blood thinner)
History: Conditions: Heart problems; Last oral intake: Earlier today (about 06:00); Notes: Patient says they can hear and understand the questions.
Red flags: Blood thinner with fall or head strike [Rule 1: Anticoagulant medication AND (fall or injury OR hit head); Medication: apixaban (Eliquis), Anticoagulant (blood thinner); Chief complaint: A fall or injury; Hit head: Yes]
Unconfirmed: None
Prototype for demonstration. Not for clinical use."
`;

