I: Location: Right arm; Facial droop (EMT): Yes; Arm drift (EMT): Yes; Speech abnormal (EMT): Yes
S: Better or worse with: Nothing changes it; Last known well: 1.5 hours ago (about 12:30); Vitals: HR 92, BP 182/98, SpO2 96%, RR 18, Glucose 118 mg/dL
T: Given: Glucose checked
Allergies: No allergies
Medications: Heart medicine, Cardiac, specific drug unknown
History: Conditions: High blood pressure; Last oral intake: A few hours (about 11:00); Notes: Patient says they can hear and understand the questions.
Red flags: Stroke alert [Rule 2: Facial droop OR arm drift OR abnormal speech; Facial droop: Yes; Arm drift: Yes; Abnormal speech: Yes; Last known well: 1.5 hours ago (about 12:30); Hours since last known well: 1.7]
Unconfirmed: None
Prototype for demonstration. Not for clinical use."
